We removed docker dependencies from kubelet /healthz a couple of releases before, so that kubelet can properly report runtime is down. But Kubelet still have a docker dependency at initial stage: 

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/cmd/kubelet/app/server.go#L150

```
	var dockerClient libdocker.Interface
	if s.ContainerRuntime == kubetypes.DockerContainerRuntime {
		dockerClient = libdocker.ConnectToDockerOrDie(s.DockerEndpoint, s.RuntimeRequestTimeout.Duration,
			s.ImagePullProgressDeadline.Duration)
	} else {
		dockerClient = nil
	}
```
We should consider removing such dependency. 

